spans.s:
इ॑तर (n. ˚रम् or ˚रद्) a. other, different from (abl.
or —˚);
 usual, common. इतरैतर the one — the other. Obs. also
द्विजेतर not a Brahman;
 सुखेतर n. pl. joy and woe;
 दक्षिणेतर
left.

इत॑स् adv. hence, from here (also इत ऊर्ध्वम्);
 from this
time, from now, henceforward (also इतो॑ ऽपरम्, इतः परम्, and इतः॑
प्रभृति);
 here, hither. इतैतः hither, hither! इतः — इतः here
— there;
 इतस्ततः here and there, hither and thither, to and fro.
इतः॑ पू॑र्वम् formerly. — Also = abl. or loc. of 1 इ.
